  "note": "One fixed reward per fault. RESOURCE adds stock to the resolving sector's real tray; INTEGRITY restores health capped at the maximum; OPPORTUNITY stores one single-use token. Nothing is rolled and nothing is chosen. A scenario's fault_reward_overrides may replace an entry with the same shape. The F-5xx reference-chain faults (2026-10-04) pay from the same table as every other fault; nothing about a chain changes what finishing one is worth.",
  "integrity_default": 5,
  "tokens": {
    "RESERVE_CREW": "+1 temporary worker for one repair procedure; declared before the repair is submitted; consumed when the attempt begins",
    "SECOND_CHANCE": "one rejected console entry does not count toward the consecutive-rejection lockout; used right after a rejected code; the code is still wrong",
    "EMERGENCY_REPAIR_KIT": "one repair procedure needs one Spare Part fewer, never below zero; declared before the repair is submitted; consumed when the attempt begins",
    "STABILISER": "blocks the next minute of one unresolved fault's integrity decay in this sector; does not resolve the fault; consumed on activation"
